  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "name": "Alicante Centro Ciudad SUMO Traffic Scenario Generation and FCD Extraction Workflow",
  "description": "A reproducible workflow for generating synthetic urban traffic demand scenarios on an OpenStreetMap-derived SUMO network of central Alicante, Spain, and for extracting Floating Car Data (FCD), including geographic coordinates and traffic-signal state, from each simulated scenario. Covers the full chain from OpenStreetMap extraction (Overpass API, Geofabrik + osmium, or pyrosm) through netconvert network conversion, randomTrips.py/duarouter-based stochastic trip generation across four vehicle-count densities (900/1000/1200/1400) with three replicates each, and SUMO microsimulation producing per-scenario FCD trajectory files. Output from this workflow is intended as the raw SUMO input to the FUMD-AI preprocessing workflow, which turns raw SUMO/OMNeT++ output into AI-ready datasets for cellular handover / migration prediction.",
